.SH NAME
ssoossh-host - Manage local sshd principal mapping, and check sshd's setup.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBssoossh host [command] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Configures the local principal mapping sshd consults through AuthorizedPrincipalsCommand: which certificate principals may log in as which local account. The mapping is a file on this host; nothing about it is stored on, or synced from, the server. Also checks that this host's sshd will accept ssoossh certificates.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--file\fP="/etc/ssoossh/principals.yaml"
	path to the local principal mapping file (YAML: local account -> list of principals)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for host


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP=""
	path to an extra config file, merged after the standard locations

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	server address, e.g. https://ssh.example.com; https is assumed when no scheme is given

.PP
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=0]
	trace what the command is doing, to stderr; repeat for more (-v steps, -vv requests and files, -vvv bodies)


